Networking Basics.
This folder covers Networking topics learnt through Jeremy's IT Lab on Youtube.

Computer Network is a Digital communications network which allows nodes to share resources.
Client is a Device that accesses a service made available by a server.
Server is a Device that provides functions or services for  a client.

NETWORKING DEVICES
SWITCHES
These are devices used to forward traffic within a LAN.
They have many interfaces/ports for end hosts to connect.
They provide connectivity to hosts within the same LAN.
They do not provide connectivity between LANs or over the internet.

ROUTERS
They have fewer network intrefaces than switches.
They are used to send data over the internet.

FIREWALL
These are special network security devices that control network traffic entering and exiting your network.
They can be inside or outside your network.
They monitor and control network traffic based on configured rules.
They are known are Next Generation Firewalls when they inlcude more modern and advanced filtering capabilities.
